{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwcHVapKyb33CeVWvQpB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't opened the dashboard or waited for the rule to run, so neither has been checked yet. The rule's status is still \"pending\".\n\n**Fields.** The data view `Kibana Sample Data Logs` (index `kibana_sample_data_logs`, time field `timestamp`) holds web-server request logs. The main fields are:\n- `response` (the HTTP status, stored as text, with a `.keyword` version)\n- `bytes`\n- `extension`\n- `clientip`\n- `geo.src` and `geo.dest`\n- `machine.os`\n- `request` and `url`\n- `agent`\n\n**Dashboard.** \"EFF-ad2bb3fe Web logs overview\" has four panels:\n- Total requests (a single number)\n- Requests over time (line chart)\n- Requests by response code (pie chart)\n- Average bytes by file extension (bar chart)\n\nIt's at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-ad2bb3fe-web-logs-overview-de78386340f7.\n\n**Alert rule.** \"EFF-ad2bb3fe 5xx spike\" (id `6a1a0418-9b28-45e6-ad2c-3278fff6bbb8`) is an Elasticsearch query rule. It runs every minute and counts documents in the last 5 minutes whose `response.keyword` matches `5[0-9][0-9]`. It fires when that count is above 10.\n\nI didn't attach any notification action, so when it fires it will only show up as an alert in Kibana."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1263,"cache_read_input_tokens":19745,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1263},"output_tokens":520,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"02e7df30-08c6-4054-850b-fb094fb59930","timestamp":"2026-10-12T03:10:15.489Z","re